1.19.0: the workspace, and recipes

The page is now a workspace: controls on the left grouped the way the
pipeline runs (scene, camera, film, development), a live preview that
re-renders on every change at the viewport's size, original / A /
current views with "pin as A" for comparing two looks on one frame, a
1:1 toggle, a strip of every image loaded this session beside the
samples, multi-file drop, keyboard glances (\ original, a A/current, r
re-render). Every element id the fake-DOM suite knows is kept.

Recipes bridge the page and the shell. A recipe is the whole look as
key=value text (docs/RECIPES.md): pj_recipe_format writes it, every
JPEG the engine saves carries it as a COM segment, and the page shows
the one it reads back from the render's bytes - the engine is the only
source of its text - with the equivalent polajuice apply line. The
page saves .recipe files, loads them or any polajuice JPEG, and keeps
named looks in local storage. The CLI: --recipe FILE (a .recipe or a
JPEG), flags after it override line by line, --save-recipe, inspect
prints an embedded recipe; superjuice --recipe; RECIPE= in super8ify,
where only knobs set explicitly go on top of it. Replay from a JPEG or
a file is byte-identical to the original render.

scripts/test_workspace.mjs drives the page in Chromium through
Playwright when it is installed (skips otherwise): render after a
click, recipe read back from the JPEG, a slider re-rendering, A/B, a
kept look surviving a reload. Added to check-wasm and the release.
